            "About thirty years later John the Baptist baptized him. The Spirit came down on him like a dove, and the Father spoke: “You are my beloved Son; with you I am well-pleased” (Mark 1:11). Then Jesus walked up to fishermen on the shore of Galilee: “Follow me” (Mark 1:17). They left their nets.",
            "For about three years he taught in the towns around that lake. He healed the sick, forgave sinners, ate with outcasts, calmed a storm and fed thousands. In his hometown synagogue he read Isaiah’s promise and said, “Today as you listen, this Scripture has been fulfilled” (Luke 4:21). Downstairs there is a fishing boat from his time, pulled from the mud of that same lake."
