            "Pontius Pilate, whose name is carved on a stone from Caesarea downstairs, found no charge that stuck, and sentenced Jesus anyway. Roman soldiers nailed him to a cross outside the city. From the cross Jesus forgave his executioners, promised paradise to a dying thief, and cried out, “It is finished” (John 19:30). Then he died.",
